From: harlan <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bmcweb: fix InsertMedia missing-credential message to say UserName

The VirtualMedia.InsertMedia action reads the credential parameter as
"UserName" (Redfish spec spelling) and logs it as such, but when it is
missing the actionParameterMissing message reported "Username" (lower-case
n).  Clients following the error message would send the wrong key and keep
getting rejected.  Make the message match the spec/JSON key.
---
 redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp
@@ -1031,7 +1031,7 @@
             BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR("Request action parameter UserName is Missing.");
 
             messages::actionParameterMissing(asyncResp->res, "InsertMedia",
-                                             "Username");
+                                             "UserName");
 
             return;
         }
